"headings":["DevExpress Unit Conversion API","When to Use This Skill","Prerequisites & Installation","NuGet Packages",".NET (8/9/10+)",".NET Framework (4.6.2+)","Package Versions","Before You Start — Ask the Developer","General Questions","Unit Conversion-Specific Questions","Component Overview","Core Entry Point — Fluent API","Core Entry Point — Units.Convert() API","Documentation & Navigation Guide","Getting Started","Quick Start Example","What This Does","Key Properties & API Surface"],"name_hint":"devexpress · office · 文件 · api · unit · conversion"},{"path":"skills/devexpress-office-file-api-word-processing/SKILL.md","name":"devexpress-office-file-api-word-processing","description":"Build .NET applications with the DevExpress Word Processing Document API for creating, reading, modifying, and exporting Word documents programmatically without Microsoft Office. Use when working with .docx, .doc, .rtf, .odt, .txt documents, paragraphs, tables, styles, mail merge, headers/footers, fields, track changes, or document conversion. Also use when someone mentions \"DevExpress Word\", \"Word Processing Document API\", \"RichEditDocumentServer\", \"DevExpress.XtraRichEdit\", \"create Word document in C#\", \"docx automation\", \"mail merge .NET\", or asks about any Word/document processing with DevExpress. Covers both .NET and .NET Framework.","headings":["DevExpress Word Processing Document API","When to Use This Skill","Prerequisites & Installation","NuGet Packages",".NET (8/9/10+)",".NET Framework (4.6.2+)","Package Versions","Non-Windows Development (Linux, macOS, Docker, Cloud)","Before You Start — Ask the Developer","General Questions","Word Processing–Specific Questions","Component Overview","Core Entry Point","Documentation & Navigation Guide","Getting Started","Getting Started — .NET Framework","Text and Paragraphs","Tables"],"name_hint":"devexpress · office · 文件 · api · word · processing"},{"path":"skills/devexpress-office-file-api-zip/SKILL.md","name":"devexpress-